arxiv-2209-04209.description:
A 2022 arXiv research paper by Gian Maria Dall’Ara, Bernhard Lamel. We prove that Heisenberg groups, a.k.a. the boundaries of Siegel domains, minimize the L p L^{p} operator norm of the Szegő projection in a large class of weighted CR manifolds of hypersurface type. Introduction

The classical Szegő projection associates to every
L^{2}
function on the boundary of a domain in
\mathbb{C}^{n}
its orthogonal projection onto the space of boundary values of holomorphic functions, that is, the Hardy space
H^{2}
.
